# 12. Visualization Graphs in the Application

The application generates several graphs to understand reservoir behavior.

---

## 12.1 Cluster Visualization

Displays wells grouped into clusters.

Each color represents a different cluster.

This helps identify production patterns among wells.

---

## 12.2 PCA Visualization

Uses **Principal Component Analysis**.

PCA reduces many parameters into two main components so complex well data can be visualized in two dimensions.

Clusters appear clearly in this graph.

---

## 12.3 3D Reservoir Visualization

Displays wells in three-dimensional space using three parameters.

Example axes:

* Reservoir Pressure
* Gas Production Rate
* Water Production Rate

This helps understand spatial relationships between wells.

---

## 12.4 Production Curve Analysis

Shows production behavior of wells within clusters.

Helps identify:

* high production wells
* declining wells
* unstable wells

---

## 12.5 Hidden Pattern Graph

Displays normal wells and anomalous wells.

Normal wells appear as blue points.
Anomalous wells appear as red markers.

These represent wells with unusual behavior.

